// Package vault turns a node record into a note file: the folder, the name, the frontmatter, the
// files a rebuild action removes, and the check that confirms or refutes one file against the node
// it records.
//
// The mapping works in both directions. The folder mirrors the package path the record carries, and
// the file name states the semantic type, the receiver when the node has one, and the node name.
// The frontmatter carries the identifier parts a location cannot carry on its own, the code region,
// and the marker that states the file was generated by the graph, which is what lets an action tell
// a file it owns from a file a person wrote.
//
// Nothing here observes the vault between actions. Each action occupies a moment: the rebuild action
// removes the files it owns and writes the files the mapping produces, and the check answers for one
// file from the file and the code at the moment it is invoked.
//
// The rules are documented in docs/vault.md.
package vault
